BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gainssa-ai-safety-essentials-fellowship-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261108
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:Deadline: GAIN SSA: AI Safety Essentials Fellowship (inaugural coho
 rt)
DESCRIPTION:GAIN SSA (Global AI Youth Network\, Sub-Saharan Africa) runs th
 e AI Safety Essentials Fellowship for residents of Africa considering how 
 they can be effective contributors in shaping the continent's transition t
 oward containing risks from transformative AI.\n\nOrganisation: GAIN SSA (
 Global AI Youth Network\, Sub-Saharan Africa)\nLocation: Online (virtual\,
  facilitated). Open to residents of African countries.\nAward: Micro-grant
  pool funding top capstone proposals at USD 500 to 1\,000 each (capped at 
 USD 1\,000)\, usable for compute access\, communication work such as Subst
 ack Pro subscriptions for writers\, or travel to AI alignment conferences 
 in Sub-Saharan Africa. The fellowship itself is free to attend (no partici
 pation fee\, no application fee)\; no stipend is paid during the program.\
 nDuration: 6-week facilitated virtual curriculum plus an onboarding pre-re
 quisites module (the site also describes it as 7 weeks)\, about 5 hours pe
 r week with one live group call per week\; capstone proposals are funded a
 fterwards\, with results within 10 days of submission.\n\nMore: https://ga
 inssa.org/initiatives/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
URL:https://gainssa.org/initiatives/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online (virtual\, facilitated). Open to residents of African count
 ries.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goethe-institut-aep-mobility-grants-2026-q2@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Deadline: Goethe-Institut: Africa-Europe Mobility Grants (15 Decemb
 er 2026 Cut-Off)
DESCRIPTION:Sub-Saharan Component (Connect & Create) of the Africa-Europe P
 artnerships for Culture programme\, an EUR 8 million 42-month initiative (
 2025-2028) implemented by the Goethe-Institut in partnership with Expertis
 e France and Institut francais. PRIMARY FOCUS: transcontinental Africa-Afr
 ica short-term mobility for artists and culture professionals.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Goethe-Institut (with Expertise France and Institut francais)\nLocat
 ion: Mobility within Sub-Saharan Africa (primary focus) and between Sub-Sa
 haran Africa and Europe\nAward: Up to EUR 4\,000 per mobility. Eligible co
 sts: travel (including visa and insurance)\, accommodation\, subsistence\,
  digital costs\, and top-up support for family\, disability\, and green mo
 bility. No application fee.\nDuration: Rolling call with quarterly cut-off
 s: 15 December 2026\, 15 March 2027\, 15 June 2027 and a final cut-off on 
 15 September 2027. Mobilities for the December cut-off take place between 
 1 January and 31 August 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.goethe.de/prj/aep/en/ca
 l/ssa/mga.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.goethe.de/prj/aep/en/cal/ssa/mga.html?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Mobility within Sub-Saharan Africa (primary focus) and between Sub
 -Saharan Africa and Europe
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-think-tanger-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Think Tanger 2027 
 (Tangier\, Morocco)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) is recruiti
 ng one Netherlands-based designer\, architect\, spatial practitioner or ma
 ker for a two-month residency in 2027 at Think Tanger\, a multidisciplinar
 y cultural platform dedicated to stimulating culture\, creativity\, innova
 tion and exchange in Tangier\, Morocco.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds
  Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL) in collaboration with T
 hink Tanger\, Morocco\nLocation: Residency takes place at Think Tanger in 
 Tangier\, Morocco. Applicants must be established in the Netherlands\, Aru
 ba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of
  the Netherlands) and registered in a business register within the Kingdom
  of the Netherlands.\nAward: EUR 5\,500 subsidy for a two-month residency\
 , paid by the Creative Industries Fund NL. No application fee.\nDuration: 
 Two months in 2027\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/ope
 n-call-residency-think-tanger?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-residency-think-ta
 nger?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at Think Tanger in Tangier\, Morocco. Applic
 ants must be established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, 
 Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and reg
 istered in a business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:playful-obscura-arthouse-games-residency-africa-2027@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T163759Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Playful Obscura 2027: Arthouse Games Residency Africa (Ad
 dis Ababa\, Goethe-Institut and A MAZE.)
DESCRIPTION:Playful Obscura is the Goethe-Institut's arthouse games residen
 cy for Africa\, co-run with the Berlin playful-media festival A MAZE. Afte
 r editions in Ho (2025) and Accra (2026)\, the third edition moves to Addi
 s Ababa with Creative HUB Ethiopia\, the British Council and Alliance Ethi
 o-Francaise.\n\nOrganisation: Goethe-Institut Addis Abeba\, with Creative 
 HUB Ethiopia\, A MAZE.\, British Council and Alliance Ethio-Francaise\nLoc
 ation: Addis Ababa\, Ethiopia. For artists and game developers based in Af
 rica working in playful media and arthouse games.\nAward: Three-week funde
 d residency hosting two artists at a time. 2027 financial terms were not p
 ublished in the call excerpt we could verify\; the 2026 Accra edition prov
 ided accommodation\, a production budget of up to EUR 1\,000 and a EUR 300
  stipend. No application fee.\nDuration: Residency 25 January to 14 Februa
 ry 2027 in Addis Ababa\; open call 16 October to 1 November 2026\, with an
  online Q&A on 22 October.\n\nMore: https://www.goethe.de/ins/za/en/kul/mu
 t/p27.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.goethe.de/ins/za/en/kul/mut/p27.html?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Addis Ababa\, Ethiopia. For artists and game developers based in A
 frica working in playful media and arthouse games.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
